e rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 45766, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PffTKx2xGaFkcZxpKm2aAy", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 45766, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PffTKx2xGaFkcZxpKm2aAy", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 47497, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RJHDK48r8P9aFoN3SWQ9Ap", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 47797, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RJHDK48r8P9aFoN3SWQ9Ap", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 47797, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RJHDK48r8P9aFoN3SWQ9Ap", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 51530, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01AjbrfLc3WNmw3gxLzpAoHn", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in every production region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.) The service was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52130, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AjbrfLc3WNmw3gxLzpAoHn", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52130, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AjbrfLc3WNmw3gxLzpAoHn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 53489, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HzPCkZ4KjFAvcxWkH9JoBE", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 53789, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HzPCkZ4KjFAvcxWkH9JoBE", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53789, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HzPCkZ4KjFAvcxWkH9JoBE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59002, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, was failing health checks and had an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in all three regions. A follow-up check shows the service is healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%. No approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. It covers the failure, the rollback, the current state, and a next step to find the cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again. It also notes that the release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was already unhealthy in staging before the production deploy. My first attempt to create the incident timed out. The incident list showed nothing had been created, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops it being created twice. There is exactly one incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MKZWsPyZMvvYTrN6244UxW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BH3AZbLCxyKUsL6rcQHRNq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01UZYJY7UdQuhTiFkJfBBq4T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GHBdr8iq9hDiA4EZip691i", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DNwce1VqR4ZfCuv9VbebZu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PffTKx2xGaFkcZxpKm2aAy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in every production region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.) The service was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RJHDK48r8P9aFoN3SWQ9Ap", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01AjbrfLc3WNmw3gxLzpAoHn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in every production region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.) The service was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HzPCkZ4KjFAvcxWkH9JoBE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, was failing health checks and had an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in all three regions. A follow-up check shows the service is healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%. No approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. It covers the failure, the rollback, the current state, and a next step to find the cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again. It also notes that the release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was already unhealthy in staging before the production deploy. My first attempt to create the incident timed out. The incident list showed nothing had been created, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops it being created twice. There is exactly one incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}